<title>BULGARIA: SOCCER-BULGARIA BEAT LUXEMBOURG 4-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BULGARIA BEAT LUXEMBOURG 4-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>BOURGAS, Bulgaria 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria beat</p>
<p>Luxembourg 4-0 (halftime 1-0) in their World Cup European group</p>
<p>five qualifier on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Hristo Stoichkov 43 pen, Emil Kostadinov 47,</p>
<p>Krasimir Balakov 50 pen, Yordan Lechkov 81</p>
<p>Attendance: 22,000</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Bulgaria: 1-Zdravko Zdravkov, 2-Anatoli Nankov, 3-Trifon</p>
<p>Ivanov, 4-Ivailo Petkov, 5-Ivailo Yordanov, 6-Zlatko Yankov</p>
<p>(14-Yordan Lechkov 58), 7-Emil Kostadinov, 8-Hristo Stoichkov,</p>
<p>9-Lyuboslav Penev (19-Daniel Borimirov 68), 10-Krasimir Balakov,</p>
<p>11-Ilian Iliev (18-Mitko Trendafilov 84)</p>
<p>Luxembourg: 1-Paul Koch, 2-Jean Vanek, 3-Frank Deville,</p>
<p>4-Marc Birsens, 5-Luc Holtz (13-Serge Thill 74), 6-Claude</p>
<p>Ganser(17-Paolo Amodio 83), 7-Guy Hellers, 8-Carlo Weis, 9-Roby</p>
<p>Langers (15-Patrick Posing 86), 10-Manuel Cardoni, 11-Dany</p>
<p>Theis.</p>
<p>    Standings  P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> Russia	  6   4   2   0  15   2    14</p>
<p> Israel	  7   4   1   2   9   6    13</p>
<p> Bulgaria	5   4   0   1  14   5    12</p>
<p> Cyprus	  6   1   1   4   5  14     4</p>
<p> Luxembourg    6   0   0   6   1  17     0</p>
<p>Next match: Aug 20 - Bulgaria v Israel</p>
</text>
